{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/weitzmanmuseum/videos/family-time-shes-a-hero-on-the-bench-and-in-the-gym/507483943461504/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/weitzmanmuseum/videos/family-time-shes-a-hero-on-the-bench-and-in-the-gym/507483943461504/","title":"Ruth Bader Ginsberg: superhero, supreme court justice, work out champion. In this video, discover how Ruth Bader Ginsberg stays healthy and active even when working from home. Want to dress like her too? Learn how to make a jabot of your own! | National Museum of American Jewish History","description":"Ruth Bader Ginsberg: superhero, supreme court justice, work out champion. In this video, discover how Ruth Bader Ginsberg stays healthy and active even when working from home. Want to dress like her...","language":"en","text":"Facebook\nLog In\nForgot Account?\nVideo\nMore\nHome\nLive\nReels\nExplore\nFamily time: She’s a hero on the bench and in the gym\nLike\nComment\nShare\n5\n·\n2 comments\n·\n430 views\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\nAccounts with a verified badge have been authenticated and can be Meta Verified subscribers or notable persons or brands.\nVerified account\nWednesday, April 8, 2020 at 12:27 PM\nApril 8, 2020\n·\nShared with Public\nFollow\nRuth Bader Ginsberg: superhero, supreme court justice, work out champion. In this video, discover ho…\nSee more\nComments\nMost relevant\n\nErica King\nLauren you’re adorable\n6y\n1\nRelated Reels\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n12K\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n671\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n9.9K\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n663\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n2.6K\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n6.2K\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n834\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n898\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n680\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n7.3K\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n658\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n\n4.4K\nRelated videos\n1:00\nWe're talking Jewish desserts. Naturally, there will be samples. 🍪 From poppy seed cookies to holiday favorites passed down through generations, some of our sweetest memories begin in the kitchen. Join Kae Lani Palmisano in conversation with Susan Spungen and Leah Koenig at The Weitzman on November 2 for A Sweet Conversation, exploring Jewish desserts, family traditions, and the stories behind the recipes we return to again and again. Reserve your spot today: https://heyor.ca/uI2Lo1\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n487 views\n·\nOctober 29 at 5:54 PM\n0:38\nWe're celebrating Sigd with a whole lot of soul! 🎶 Join us November 8 as Gili Yalo takes the stage at The Weitzman for a special Secret Chord Concert honoring the Ethiopian Jewish holiday of Sigd. Blending Ethiopian traditions with funk, soul, and psychedelic sounds, Gili brings an unforgettable energy to the stage. Grab your tickets today: https://heyor.ca/s6PkLx\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n1.5K views\n·\nOctober 20 at 2:00 PM\n0:09\nOn October 21, we're setting the table for our annual Women's Leadership Forum Luncheon at The Weitzman, featuring New York Times bestselling author Catherine Ostler. Join as we celebrate inspiring and influential women leaders in the Jewish community with a catered lunch, a VIP museum tour, and a conversation with Catherine about 'The Renoir Girls,' and the real women whose lives inspired her latest book: https://heyor.ca/MLuQ5i\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n799 views\n·\nOctober 14 at 3:04 PM\n0:23\nSaturday Night Live premiered on this day in 1975, with Jewish American comedian Gilda Radner among its original cast. Roseanne Roseannadanna. Baba Wawa. Emily Litella. Gilda’s characters became part of SNL and comedy history. 51 years later, which Gilda character still gets you every time? 😂👇 (🎥: Love Gilda | Original SNL footage: NBC)\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n324.4K views\n·\nOctober 11 at 1:01 PM\n0:30\nTo remember is to bear witness. Three years after October 7, Nova music festival survivor Natalie Sanandaji reminds us of something each of us can do: listen to the stories of those who were there, and make sure what happened is known. Today, we remember the lives lost on October 7, honor those forever changed, and make space for the voices carrying their experiences forward.\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n1.1K views\n·\nOctober 7 at 8:30 AM\n0:21\nAll the colors. All the feels. Now FREE. 🌈 Step inside the \"Colors of Creation,\" our immersive family experience filled with movement, music, play, and plenty of wonder for everyone. Don't miss it while it's free for a limited time! Plan your visit today: https://heyor.ca/95HGqj #WeitzmanColors #MuseumEducation #PhillyKids #PhillySchools #KidFriendlyPhilly #FamilyFunAtTheWeitzman\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n474 views\n·\nOctober 6\n0:44\nWhat can one shofar tell us about Jewish American life more than a century ago? 🔎 For William Cohen, it was part of a daily ritual during Elul. For his daughter Elizabeth, it became part of her memories of growing up in a deeply Jewish home. And today, it helps us tell the story of Jewish life taking root in rural South Jersey. Hear the story from The Weitzman’s President & CEO, Dan Tadmor, then discover more during your next trip to The Weitzman: https://heyor.ca/3e9dPU\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n751 views\n·\nSeptember 28\n1:18\nStart the season with an evening of Jewish joy! ✨ On September 8th, Rebekah Lowin and Jennifer Weiner celebrate the launch of 'A Year of Jewish Joy,' bringing recipes, reflections, and inspiration together as we look ahead to Rosh Hashanah and the new year. Come early to explore the galleries before the 7 PM program, then stay for book-inspired bites and a meet-and-greet! Grab your tickets now: https://heyor.ca/Gyw1Ef\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n6.1K views\n·\nSeptember 3\n0:21\nWe love a unanimous family review. 🌈 Step into a colorful, immersive experience made for exploring, playing, and finding a little wonder—together. Come see what the hype is about. Plan your visit to \"Colors of Creation\" at The Weitzman: https://heyor.ca/ZRUrq7\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\n586 views\n·\nAugust 24\nPages\nBusinesses\nArts & entertainment\nMuseum\nHistory Museum\nNational Museum of American Jewish History\nVideos\nFamily time: She’s a hero on the bench and in the gym\nView Transcript\nHome\nLive\nExplore\nSee more on Facebook\nEmail or phone number\nPassword\nLog In\nForgot password?\nor\nCreate new account","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2559.4700259971432,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}